# Normalize every text file to LF in the index and on checkout.
#
# The runtime's golden/parity tests (runtime/tests/golden/*.jsonl,
# runtime/tests/parity/) byte-compare captured streams against tracked
# files, and the markdown fixtures under runtime/tests/fixtures/ feed
# byte-sensitive frontmatter parsing. A CRLF checkout (Windows runners
# default to core.autocrlf=true) would break those comparisons, so LF is
# pinned repo-wide rather than per-path.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The archive /ductus downloads carries only the files a run reads (spec 015
# AC14). GitHub builds the codeload tarball with `git archive`, which leaves
# out every path marked export-ignore in the archived commit's own copy of
# this file. Everything is marked, framework/ and the one manifest source
# outside it are unmarked, and the framework/ files no run reads are marked
# again. /audit Family 42 (scripts/audit/archive-contents.sh) holds this list
# to the installer in both directions, so a file a run newly reads that is
# marked here, or a new path a run never reads that is not, fails it.
* export-ignore
/framework -export-ignore
/framework/** -export-ignore
/.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc -export-ignore
# Fetched by pre-rename adopters from raw.githubusercontent.com, never from
# the archive (049; /audit Family 21 keeps it identical to ductus.md).
/framework/bootstrap/govern.md export-ignore
# The generator and test input for the MCP tool list.
/framework/runtime-tools.txt export-ignore
# Copied into an adopter's CI by hand; no run writes it.
/framework/templates/ci/adopter-generators.yml export-ignore
# The maintainer-only command and its reference, withheld from adopters
# (scripts/maintainer-only-commands.txt).
/framework/commands/audit.md export-ignore
/framework/reference/audit.md export-ignore
